# Tasks — GetYourRide Live Tracking Build Plan

This document outlines the phased build plan for adding live trip tracking + simulation to GetYourRide. Each phase maps to a git branch, lists deliverables, specifies what gets checked/tested, and defines acceptance criteria before moving to the next phase.

> Backend repo: `kelvin-2/GetYourRide_backend`. Related docs: [`GetYourRide_Tracking_Documentation.md`](GetYourRide_Tracking_Documentation.md) for full API + architecture reference.

## Branch Strategy

```mermaid
gitGraph
    commit id: "main"
    branch step-0-db-cleanup
    commit id: "migration + fixes"
    branch step-1-validation-fixes
    commit id: "close the 0,0 bug"
    branch step-2-route-wiring
    commit id: "real coords in RouteController"
    branch step-3-leg-precompute
    commit id: "trip_leg_route population"
    branch step-4-websocket
    commit id: "STOMP infra"
    branch step-5-scheduler
    commit id: "simulation engine"
    branch step-6-android-tracking
    commit id: "TrackingScreen"
    branch step-7-polish
    commit id: "UX + testing"
```

Each branch should be independently testable before merging to `main` — don't start a phase until the previous one's acceptance criteria are all checked.

