## Phase 3 — WebSocket / STOMP Infrastructure

**Branch:** `step-4-websocket`

**Objective:** Add the real-time transport layer that doesn't exist yet in the repo.

**Deliverables:**
- `WebSocketConfig` registering a STOMP endpoint (e.g. `/ws`) with a simple broker on `/topic`
- `LocationUpdateDTO` and `StopEventDTO` message classes
- A test publisher (manually triggered) to confirm messages reach a subscribed client before the scheduler exists

**What to check first:**
- [ ] Confirm Spring Boot has `spring-boot-starter-websocket` as a dependency (check `pom.xml`/`build.gradle`)
- [ ] Test the endpoint with `wscat` or Postman's WebSocket support before writing any Android client code

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] A client can subscribe to `/topic/trip/{tripId}` and receive a manually-published test message
- [ ] Message shapes match the documented JSON in `GetYourRide_Tracking_Documentation.md` §4.4

