## Phase 6 — Polish + Testing

**Branch:** `step-7-polish`

**Objective:** Handle edge cases, connection loss, and general UX rough edges before calling tracking "done."

**Deliverables:**
- WebSocket reconnection handling (auto-retry, visible "reconnecting" state)
- Fallback: if STOMP fails entirely, poll `GET /api/trips/{id}` on an interval instead
- Recenter FAB button, camera-follow logic that doesn't fight the user's manual pan
- Secrets moved out of `application.properties` into environment variables
- End-to-end test: full simulated trip from start to completion, verified visually on device

**What to check first:**
- [ ] Kill the WebSocket connection mid-trip (airplane mode toggle) and confirm the app recovers without crashing
- [ ] Confirm database credentials/API keys are no longer visible in the committed `application.properties`

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] App recovers gracefully from a dropped connection
- [ ] No secrets remain committed to the repo
- [ ] A full simulated trip (multiple stops) runs start-to-finish without manual intervention
- [ ] Map UI matches the agreed visual direction (clean markers, dual polyline, bottom sheet — see mockup)

